WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.489 --> 00:00:05.181
DC's Deathstroke has enjoyed a resurgence
the past few years thanks in large part to

00:00:05.181 --> 00:00:06.559
the CW's Arrow.

00:00:06.559 --> 00:00:11.419
As we settle in for Joe Manganiello's version
of the character in the DC Extended Universe,

00:00:11.419 --> 00:00:15.969
we're taking a deep dive into the character
and offering a few tidbits you might not know

00:00:15.969 --> 00:00:20.390
about one of DC Comics' greatest tacticians
and most dangerous villains.

00:00:20.390 --> 00:00:23.270
Here's the untold truth of Deathstroke.

00:00:23.270 --> 00:00:25.060
Original Terminator

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:29.480
Though he's likely best known for his more
recent work, especially his roles on Arrow

00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:33.540
and the upcoming Batman film, Deathstroke
has been causing trouble in the comics for

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:35.250
almost 40 years.

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:40.680
Slade Wilson was first introduced in New Teen
Titans #2, which was released in December

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:41.680
1980.

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:44.690
At the time, he was known as Deathstroke:
the Terminator.

00:00:44.690 --> 00:00:50.010
His first appearance came four years before
James Cameron's Terminator, but by the mid-'80s,

00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:55.070
most people associated the name with a time-traveling
Arnold Schwarzenegger, regardless of who came

00:00:55.070 --> 00:00:56.070
first.

00:00:56.070 --> 00:01:01.030
DC opted to quietly retire the "Terminator"
subtitle and just stick with Deathstroke.

00:01:01.030 --> 00:01:05.700
In the years since, he's taken shots at just
about every DC hero in the books.

00:01:05.700 --> 00:01:07.060
For example...

00:01:07.060 --> 00:01:09.100
He beat up the Justice League

00:01:09.100 --> 00:01:13.620
The Justice League may be DC's Mightiest Heroes,
but they still need to watch out for Deathstroke.

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:19.479
As part of DC's Identity Crisis storyline
in 2004, Slade was employed as the bodyguard

00:01:19.479 --> 00:01:20.780
for Doctor Light.

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:24.930
Since that involved protecting him from a
large contingent of the Justice League, Deathstroke

00:01:24.930 --> 00:01:29.799
strategized how to take down each separate
member, and systematically started neutralizing

00:01:29.799 --> 00:01:30.799
them.

00:01:30.799 --> 00:01:35.420
He faced off against a team comprised of the
Green Lantern, the Flash, Green Arrow, Atom,

00:01:35.420 --> 00:01:39.010
Hawkman, Zatanna, Elongated Man, and Black
Canary.

00:01:39.010 --> 00:01:43.930
It was working pretty well...until Green Arrow
jammed an arrow through his eye and sent him

00:01:43.930 --> 00:01:44.930
into a blind rage.

00:01:44.930 --> 00:01:49.479
At that point, he just started pounding on
Green Arrow, which gave the rest of the team

00:01:49.479 --> 00:01:52.420
an opening to tackle him to the ground and
stop the fight.

00:01:52.420 --> 00:01:53.819
So close, Slade.

00:01:53.819 --> 00:01:54.999
So close.

00:01:54.999 --> 00:01:56.869
He defeated the X-Men

00:01:56.869 --> 00:02:02.490
In times past, DC and Marvel weren't afraid
to crossover for some truly insane—and fun—comics

00:02:02.490 --> 00:02:03.490
events.

00:02:03.490 --> 00:02:07.679
Deathstroke got his chance to prowl around
the Marvel Comics universe as part of Marvel

00:02:07.679 --> 00:02:13.180
and DC's The Uncanny X-Men and The New Teen
Titans one-off, which found the Titans and

00:02:13.180 --> 00:02:15.290
X-Men teaming up to stop Darkseid.

00:02:15.290 --> 00:02:19.740
But the Titans brought along their most famous
nemesis for the ride, who took out both the

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:22.150
Titans and the X-Men along the way.

00:02:22.150 --> 00:02:25.740
Not even Wolverine and Colossus could defeat
him when the battle started.

00:02:25.740 --> 00:02:30.090
It just proved again that he's a force to
be reckoned with—no matter what comics universe

00:02:30.090 --> 00:02:31.140
he's in.

00:02:31.140 --> 00:02:33.140
He inspired Deadpool

00:02:33.140 --> 00:02:37.280
You don't have to look much further than their
names, skill sets, and outfits to realize

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:41.070
that Deathstroke and Deadpool have maybe a
few things in common.

00:02:41.070 --> 00:02:45.570
Well, there's a good reason for that: Deadpool
is basically an homage to Deathstroke, just

00:02:45.570 --> 00:02:47.660
with more of an attitude.

00:02:47.660 --> 00:02:49.330
"I know, right?"

00:02:49.330 --> 00:02:55.190
Deadpool co-creators Fabian Nicieza and Rob
Liefeld were reportedly big fans of Deathstroke,

00:02:55.190 --> 00:02:59.190
so they borrowed from their fan favorite when
putting together the pitch for Wade Wilson.

00:02:59.190 --> 00:03:03.320
In fairness, the characters diverged quite
a lot once Deadpool's story developed.

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:04.380
Liefeld said:

00:03:04.380 --> 00:03:07.500
"While ruthless, there is certain nobility
to Slade.

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:11.490
He tried to have a normal family at one point,
and believed in honor amongst thieves.

00:03:11.490 --> 00:03:14.230
Wade, while canny, is an insane person.

00:03:14.230 --> 00:03:18.200
The similarities are they both shoot guns
and wield swords."

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:19.460
Family ties

00:03:19.460 --> 00:03:24.110
Unlike a lot of comic book villains, Slade
Wilson is also a family man—and his family

00:03:24.110 --> 00:03:27.320
has also crossed paths with the Teen Titans
several times.

00:03:27.320 --> 00:03:29.880
In almost every case, it didn't go well.

00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:32.350
His son Grant cut a deal with the evil H.I.V.E.

00:03:32.350 --> 00:03:36.750
for enhanced abilities to take out the young
heroes, but the enhancements taxed Grant's

00:03:36.750 --> 00:03:39.940
body too much, and he died in his father's
arms.

00:03:39.940 --> 00:03:43.880
Slade's second son, Joseph, was kidnapped
and had his throat slit while Deathstroke

00:03:43.880 --> 00:03:45.370
was trying to rescue him.

00:03:45.370 --> 00:03:50.240
Joseph survived, but the injury severed his
vocal cords, leaving him unable to speak.

00:03:50.240 --> 00:03:54.280
Slade's wife, upset over the whole ordeal,
shot him in the face and damaged his eye.

00:03:54.280 --> 00:03:58.990
And that's not all: his daughter Rose became
a villain under the adopted mantle Ravager.

00:03:58.990 --> 00:04:01.950
Guess villainy just runs in the Wilson family.

00:04:01.950 --> 00:04:03.220
Hail to the chief

00:04:03.220 --> 00:04:08.650
An alternate version of Deathstroke is introduced
in DC's animated film Justice League: Crisis

00:04:08.650 --> 00:04:09.650
on Two Earths.

00:04:09.650 --> 00:04:13.820
In this world, Slade has gone into politics
and climbed the ladder to become the President

00:04:13.820 --> 00:04:15.470
of the United States.

00:04:15.470 --> 00:04:20.169
Unsurprisingly, the guy's a pretty badass
POTUS, leading U.S. forces alongside the Justice

00:04:20.169 --> 00:04:22.219
League to battle the Syndicate.

00:04:22.219 --> 00:04:26.821
Interestingly, this Slade has an eyepatch
on his left eye instead of the right, since

00:04:26.821 --> 00:04:29.680
he's sort of a mirror version in this world.

00:04:29.680 --> 00:04:30.680
Not that it matters.

00:04:30.680 --> 00:04:32.039
Eyepatches are always cool.

00:04:32.039 --> 00:04:33.610
"You can't see it.

00:04:33.610 --> 00:04:35.169
I just winked."

00:04:35.169 --> 00:04:36.280
Thanks for watching!

00:04:36.280 --> 00:04:39.259
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:04:39.259 --> 00:04:41.349
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

